{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1377310-how-to-use-prime-magic-for-assassination","id":1377310,"title":"How to use Prime magic for assassination.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-30T01:12:39-07:00","id":1377310,"title":"How to use Prime magic for assassination.","content":"I was planning on playing a mage assassin with 4 prime. I was going to use platonic form for extreemly powerful 7 +damage throwing knives, and wards and signs for defense. Any other ways you can think of to use prime to quickly defeat another mage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T01:24:02-07:00","id":1377311,"title":"","content":"Creative application of Supernal Dispellation works wonders against other mages. If you dip into Fate you could have Supernal Dispellation as an AoE effect (possibly on a throwing knife to get rid of those pesky wards) while using Warding Gesture to exempt your own spells. Fate is also great for minimising trouble on the way to the target and finding them in disadventageous situations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T07:40:06-07:00","id":1377341,"title":"","content":"Prime is great for it, some immediate uses that come to mind (apart from dispellation):<br /> <br /> 1- Wards &amp; Signs is great to defend yourself or your proxies (warded Sleepers with guns are terribly effective against mages). <br /> 2- Supernal Veil, because if their peripheral sight doesn't ping, it means you can setup lots of traps.<br /> 3- Cloak Nimbus, because if your target cannot know where the attack comes from or who setup the trap, then the psychological effect is heightened. <br /> 4- Pierce Deception, because a wary target may try subterfuge against you.<br /> 5- Retexturing objects using Veiling, it can lead to subtle trickery (refer to Hisoka from HunterXHunter and the Reality Makers Legacy for examples).<br /> 6- Platonic forms of weird combined properties, for example Hisoka's Bungee Gum ability<br /> 7- Lots of imbued items. They allow for scalability (with enough mana you could arguably affect the entire world and still only use one spell slot) and high spell factors on command. Words of Command means you can use them far more reliably than anyone else.<br /> 8- Nimbus Forgery, because sometimes tensions are so high and a target is so willing to believe their enemy/rival/adversary did something that they forget to apply due diligence to the evidence. Sometimes all you need is to give someone an excuse and they will escalate things.<br /> 9- Stored spells to let your cabalmates prepare some rapid fire buffs. Pair it with a Mastigos's Space magic and a Prime version of Remote Control to create a rapid fire damage burst.<br /> 10- Make the target seem like a crazed liar by Veiling the truth with a reverse Words of Truth (&quot;Help, someone is trying to take me out&quot; &quot;Sure they are buddy, sure they are&quot;). This might need Mind/Fate to fine tune to specific topics, otherwise it will be very suspicious that the person suddenly became a &quot;blatant pathological liar&quot;<br /> <br /> With major political goodwill with the Mysterium, Guardians or Arrow, its arguably possible that they could have a Timori Daimonomikon for black ops agents. But this would probably come with major political and supernatural strings attached, like having a summoned Fate entity seal an oath not to use your Attainments on Pentacle or Nameless mages without sanction, with a rule of 3 escalating fate based punishments. That is in addition to becoming an ageless thaumavore with a crystalized body, but nothing ventured, nothing gained.<br /> <br /> Lastly, if you just want to play an assassin and Prime is not necessarily a requirement, then I also recommend the Nizari:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1281000-help-with-custom-legacy-the-nizari\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...acy-the-nizari</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 03-30-2020, 11:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T07:49:46-07:00","id":1377342,"title":"","content":"A note on point 7: The AoE part of Scale is capped so no spells over the whole world. Not to mention that every single mage in the whole world would notice (or have a chance to notice, if it's Veiled), as well as archmasters and similarly powerful beings, and that there's probably at least one artefact or other goodie out there that just shuts down the spell if it would become a subject. Oh, and there are things that cause paradox when casting certain spells on them.<br /> I know it was a hyperbole. I just started thinking about all the various things that could and would ruin yourbday if you tried.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T08:06:44-07:00","id":1377344,"title":"","content":"I wonder if it's possible to cast Platonic Form on a target, weaving a Mana-bullet or poison or such directly into their body. It would probably be Withstood by Stamina.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T08:08:14-07:00","id":1377345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1377310-how-to-use-prime-magic-for-assassination?p=1377342#post1377342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A note on point 7: The AoE part of Scale is capped so no spells over the whole world. Not to mention that every single mage in the whole world would notice (or have a chance to notice, if it's Veiled), as well as archmasters and similarly powerful beings, and that there's probably at least one artefact or other goodie out there that just shuts down the spell if it would become a subject. Oh, and there are things that cause paradox when casting certain spells on them.<br /> I know it was a hyperbole. I just started thinking about all the various things that could and would ruin yourbday if you tried.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see how that could be misinterpreted as Imperial Magic level scale, my bad. I just meant that no matter how many times you activate an imbued item, it only costs one spell slot. So if a mage was crazy enough and had enough mana, nothing stops them from letting the entire city or Consillium from benefiting from it. <br /> <br /> Its certainly expensive resource wise and there are caveats, but its still a pretty good cost benefit when it comes to scalability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T09:40:24-07:00","id":1377357,"title":"","content":"Platonic forming cyanide or some other poison directly into someones food or drink has to come up at least once. Once the spells duration expires, the poisons gone! Perfect crime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T09:51:56-07:00","id":1377359,"title":"","content":"Platonic Form isn't very subtle unless you pair it with other magic. It's usually obviously magical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T11:27:28-07:00","id":1377375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1377310-how-to-use-prime-magic-for-assassination?p=1377359#post1377359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Platonic Form isn't very subtle unless you pair it with other magic. It's usually obviously magical.</div> </div> </div> </div>What are some uses for platonic form. It mostly makes simple weapons right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T11:36:37-07:00","id":1377376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\