ersion of Remote Control to create a rapid fire damage burst.<br /> 10- Make the target seem like a crazed liar by Veiling the truth with a reverse Words of Truth (&amp;quot;Help, someone is trying to take me out&amp;quot; &amp;quot;Sure they are buddy, sure they are&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. This might need Mind/Fate to fine tune to specific topics, otherwise it will be very suspicious that the person suddenly became a &amp;quot;blatant pathological liar&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> With major political goodwill with the Mysterium, Guardians or Arrow, its arguably possible that they could have a Timori Daimonomikon for black ops agents. But this would probably come with major political and supernatural strings attached, like having a summoned Fate entity seal an oath not to use your Attainments on Pentacle or Nameless mages without sanction, with a rule of 3 escalating fate based punishments. That is in addition to becoming an ageless thaumavore with a crystalized body, but nothing ventured, nothing gained.<br /> <br /> Lastly, if you just want to play an assassin and Prime is not necessarily a requirement, then I also recommend the Nizari:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1281000-help-with-custom-legacy-the-nizari&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...acy-the-nizari</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Can you explain 9. It went over my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T12:50:47-07:00","id":1377386,"title":"","content":"Sure thing. First you place a bunch of attack spells in an item using Stored Spell. Then you do the Prime equivalent of Remote Control to activate it at a distance. <br /> <br /> Now you have a Space mage Co-locate/Teleport them so they touch the target. You spend a mana to activate and boom, all those touch attack spells go off at once.<br /> <br /> So lets say you have a cabal of 3 Gnosis and Arcanum 3 mages, including yourself. <br /> <br /> So you made 2 Potency 3 Stored Spell pieces of paper that last a week. For your last spell slot you make a 2 target remote trigger spell.<br /> <br /> The Mastigos opens the co-location and stores 2 attack spells and decides to over Reach to store a third. <br /> <br /> The third cabalmate stores 3 attack spells.<br /> <br /> Now you teleport the pieces of paper so they touch the target, spend 2 mana to use the stored spells and boom, 18 damage. This is without even considering your cabalmates using yantras.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 03-30-2020, 03:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T17:33:15-07:00","id":1377413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1377310-how-to-use-prime-magic-for-assassination?p=1377386#post1377386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure thing. First you place a bunch of attack spells in an item using Stored Spell. Then you do the Prime equivalent of Remote Control to activate it at a distance. <br /> <br /> Now you have a Space mage Co-locate/Teleport them so they touch the target. You spend a mana to activate and boom, all those touch attack spells go off at once.<br /> <br /> So lets say you have a cabal of 3 Gnosis and Arcanum 3 mages, including yourself. <br /> <br /> So you made 2 Potency 3 Stored Spell pieces of paper that last a week. For your last spell slot you make a 2 target remote trigger spell.<br /> <br /> The Mastigos opens the co-location and stores 2 attack spells and decides to over Reach to store a third. <br /> <br /> The third cabalmate stores 3 attack spells.<br /> <br /> Now you teleport the pieces of paper so they touch the target, spend 2 mana to use the stored spells and boom, 18 damage. This is without even considering your cabalmates using yantras.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. Thats terrifying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T19:00:23-07:00","id":1377430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1377310-how-to-use-prime-magic-for-assassination?p=1377375#post1377375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are some uses for platonic form. It mostly makes simple weapons right?</div> </div> </div> </div>There\u2019s a Reach option to allow for complicated devices. I\u2019d probably still limit those to being purely mechanical though. Like a gun is probably fine, but you\u2019d need actual bullets for it to fire.<br /> <br /> The main \u201cproblem\u201d is that anything you make will be obviously magical and trigger Quiescence and Dissonance. It\u2019s still very versatile though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 03-30-2020, 10:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T09:57:23-07:00","id":1377527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1377310-how-to-use-prime-magic-for-assassination?p=1377413#post1377413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow. Thats terrifying.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be if it was possible. Direct damage spells have been clarified to be subject to spell stacking, so only the most potent one to hit them on the turn you trigger the device would actually apply its effects.<br /> <br /> You would have to stagger their application somehow for this to work - but honestly, direct damage spells are the most boring way to approach this pretty ingenious deployment mechanism - I think you'd get a lot more mileage out of it with other hostile magic, instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T11:47:13-07:00","id":1377544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/908138-combined-attack-spells-for-double-damage?p=921960#post921960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, it's being adjusted for clarity in the errata pass, but the idea is that Combined spells use their overall Potency for each &quot;spell&quot;, but if the spells do the same thing they don't stack.<br /> <br /> So if you combine a life 3 direct attack with a reach for inflicting arm wrack with a mind 4 direact attack doing lethal, you end up with potency in lethal plus arm wrack. The greater damage spell &quot;wins&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the closest thing I could find to that clarification. It seems it only applies to combined spells. But I couldn't find any other reference to per turn damage limits, so stored and hung spells should still be usable for burst damage. <br /> <br /> Its basic and will certainly not be as good as applying conditions on stronger foes, but its still a decent tool for simple assassinations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T12:24:31-07:00","id":1377555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When multiple spells affect the same aspect of a character the effects of the spells do not stack, and instead the spell with the highest Potency takes effect. </div> </div> </div><s> imo, by any reasonable definition, direct damage spells all 'affect the same aspect of a character'. </s><br /> <br /> <s> It's not an issue if they're staggered because then by the time the second spell hits, the first is no longer actively affecting them. </s><br /> <br /> Edit: After some discussion in Discord, I think it may actually be reasonable to treat damage, healing, and other instantaneous, Lasting effects differently. It'd probably work out as described.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 03-31-2020, 05:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}